## Open Questions
Wording alone is a weak fix for the comment-artifact problem, and I told Aaron
so. The failure is that the model does not revisit its own comments late in a
long session, and a sentence read at the start loses to recency. The durable fix
is a check at the end — a verification skill or a stop hook that rereads the
session's added comments against the final diff. He has not asked for it. If he
raises the problem again, build that rather than rewording the paragraph.

Whether 97 lines of always-on writing guidance is the right size. It is the
